Public Services and Procurement Canada is the proponent, administrator of lands and funder to provide and install a site wide security camera system at Esquimalt Graving Dock (EGD). This includes security lighting, new anchored poles, low-voltage power supply and distribution, telecommunication distribution and related auxiliary equipment for a fully functional efficient surveillance system at EGD. Excavation will be required for the installation of 21 light pole bases (total of 24 light poles) and 2 trenches for the installation of underground electrical and communication conduits are required to install concrete light base and new underground conduits (duct banks).&nbsp; The total footprint of the project is 542.25 square meters.

&nbsp;

Esquimalt Graving Dock (EGD) is a 31-hectare federal shipyard facility located in Skinner Cove, Esquimalt Harbour, B.C. and was constructed over 7 years, starting operation in 1927. Property borders include a residential area, another federal property (Department of National Defence, DND), Songhees First Nations lands and the marine environment (Esquimalt Harbour).&nbsp; The property is developed with active shipyard infrastructure with some natural vegetation areas. Some portions of the site are listed as active on the Federal Contaminated Sites Inventory (FCSI).

&nbsp;

Latitude and longitude: 48.427&deg; N, 123.381&deg; W

